#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0141 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "THE UN-GATE PIN (Fix #340, owner ruling 2026-08-22 under EC-86: CDISC-SEND-0141 is bucket 1, UN-GATE). Fix #331 had gated this rule on Requirements.Variables.All [DSTERM, DSDECOD]; the ruling reversed that, and the whole Variables block is gone. DS declares DSTERM populated on both rows and NO DSDECOD column at all. Under absent = all-missing (Fix #330) empty(DSDECOD) is TRUE on every row, the sibling not empty(DSTERM) holds, so the rule fires on BOTH rows - the strongest form of the defect the rule exists for (nothing was ever mapped to CT). Re-add either All entry and this goes SKIPPED instead; if that happens the un-gate was reverted -- escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 DSSEQ=1 USUBJID=S1-001
dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | S1-001 | 1 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE
S1 | DS | S1-002 | 2 | FOUND DEAD
---
